code 'extract entities' :: (input: string) -> [Entity]:
```bpl
pragma(temperature=0.5, max_tokens=1024, model=context["text-davinci-003"])
# Task metadata
"task \"extract entities\"\n"
"Extract the distinct entities from the text\n"

# Task type instruction
"func extract entities {\n"
"  input: string\n"
"  output: Entity[]\n"
"}\n"

"struct Entity {\n"
"  name: string # \"Canonical name of the entity\"\n"
"  type: EntityType\n"
"  confidence: number | null # \"Confidence in the detected type\"\n"
"}\n"

"confidence: number | null # \"Confidence in the detected type\"\n"

"enum EntityType {\n"
"  \"PER\" # \"Person\"\n"
"  \"LOC\" # \"Location\"\n"
"  \"ORG\" # \"Organization\"\n"
"  \"MISC\" # \"Misc\"\n"
"}\n"

# Task inference
"Perform the task extract entities as described above to complete the output with the correct types. Consider the instructions carefully:\n"
"Extract the distinct entities from the text\n"
" - The entities are distinct\n"
# Task type example stub
"The data should look like this (with real values obviously):\n"
"{ \n"
"  \"input\": "
"string"
",\n"
"  \"output\": "
"  [ \n"
"    { \n"
"      \"name\": "
"string"
"    ,\n"
"      \"type\": "
"PER"
"    ,\n"
"      \"confidence\": "
"7"
"    ,\n"
"    }\n"
"  ,\n"
"  ]\n"
",\n"
"}\n"

"{\n"
"  \"input\": \"{input}\",\n"
final_output = []
"  \"output\": [\n"
while True:
    "  "
    "[cont: `\" \"` | `\"\{\"` | `\"\]\"`]"
    if cont == ']':
        break
    elif cont == ' ':
        " "
    elif cont == '{':
        "\n"
    "    \"name\": [name: string],\n"
    "    \"type\": [type: EntityType],\n"
    "    \"confidence\": [confidence: number | null],\n"
    element = Entity(name=name, type=type, confidence=confidence)
    "  }"
    final_output.append(element)
"}"
return final_output
```
